# Direct historical theorem reading after audit1575

Read [hep-th/9409094v1](https://arxiv.org/html/hep-th/9409094v1), TheoremsIII.1/III.2/IV.5 and selected proof paragraphs. III.1 uses globally smooth Banach-valued functions on real edge space, with distinct-edge derivatives evaluated at path-minimum forest points. IV.5 gives positivity through convex combinations of block-diagonal pinchings. The source explicitly warns that the alternative rooted interpolation does not preserve positivity. The full upstream algebraic proof chain was not audited.

Use III.1, together with the finite smooth extension, for the conditional Gaussian dictionary. A root in a polymer norm is not permission to replace that interpolation by III.2. The pinching mechanism is classical1994 literature, not a new result or separate paper.

This new parent reading is outside audit1575 and the fixed PR241 head. Its frozen F4 statement remains historically accurate. Queue a reading-depth update to the existing source card after publication closure. No source-law, spatial-summation, normalization or full complex-domain gate is discharged.

Levels: literature—selected statements/proof paragraphs; heuristic—application dictionary; formal—no import/build; speculative—full source transfer. Falsifier: a mismatch of smoothness/domain or interpolation choice.
